    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38528" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōcurso</span></b> , āre,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq.
			n.</i> [id.], <i>to run forth</i>, <i>to
				sally out</i>, <i>make attacks</i> or <i>onsets.</i> —Of skirmishers: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum ab stationibus procursaretur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 5, 5, § 15</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 10,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to advance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in pulcra facinora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 6, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
